   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Gas accumulation around the TAC can result in gas interference and gas locking the subsurface pump.",
   "box": {
    "x": 730,
    "y": 249,
    "w": 467,
    "h": 50
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Seating Nipple",
   "box": {
    "x": 440,
    "y": 293,
    "w": 124,
    "h": 42
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "These problems negatively affect the operating efficiency of the pumping system and can result in long-term damage to the pumping system components.",
   "box": {
    "x": 730,
    "y": 325,
    "w": 467,
    "h": 76
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "One of the areas where gas accumulation can be particularly troublesome is around the TAC.",
   "box": {
    "x": 730,
    "y": 425,
    "w": 467,
    "h": 50
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Odessa Separator, Inc. has developed a TAC with a gas vent that prevents gas accumulation below the TAC while providing an effective tubing anchor. Available in both standard and “slim-line” TAC’s, the OSI Gas Vent TAC increases annular flow area by 250% and 35% respectively.",
   "box": {
    "x": 730,
    "y": 476,
    "w": 467,
    "h": 151
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Employing patented OSI “Dual-Flow” technology, the Gas Vent TAC can be combined with any gas separator and any other OSI fluid conditioning tools.",
   "box": {
    "x": 730,
    "y": 652,
    "w": 467,
    "h": 76
